# Kanban Workflow (Jager-C2)

Full rules: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) section "Kanban board workflow".

## Board

GitHub Projects board "Jager-C2 Roadmap" linked in README. Columns:
Backlog -> Ready -> In Progress (max 1 per agent) -> In Review -> Done.

## Labels

- Priority: `priority/p1`, `priority/p2`, `priority/p3`
- Area: `area/teamserver`, `area/implant`, `area/mcp`, `area/builder`, `area/cli`, `area/ci`, `area/docs`
- Type: `bug`, `enhancement`, `documentation`, `good first issue`

## Agent loop

1. Pick the highest-priority unassigned item in Ready: `gh issue list -R 0xhackerfren/Jager-C2`
2. Assign yourself, move to In Progress
3. Work; if blocked, comment on the issue and move back to Ready
4. PR with `Fixes #N`; CI green; card to In Review
5. Merge: card to Done, issue closes

## Rules

- One item in progress per agent
- Too-large tasks get split into child issues referencing the parent
- New discovered work becomes an issue with labels, never just a commit message
- Project commands (`gh project ...`) require the `project` scope on the gh token